    "Scouting Notes": "POST DRAFT NOTES\n A nice 6 foot 6, 200 pound frame to work with\n Fantastic freshman year at Duke, solid Sophomore year (was a T300 prospect in 2024 class per BA), but major struggles in his Junior season\n Fastball sits 92–94 MPH, touches 97 MPH with decent shape\n Changeup is his best secondary IMO, has good shape and kills velo pretty well too\n Slider came along later in his college career, but is inconsistent. He spins it well, and I think it could be an above average pitch\n Curveball is more of a WIP, but again, the feel for spin makes me think he can get to fringe average or better\n Reminds me a bit of Tate Kuehner coming out of Louisville\n Despite the struggles his final season, think there's a SP profile here",
